# THIN DOSSIER, CREDITS ONLY: no artist page, no biography, no interview and no official account under this name was found on any platform consulted. The verified public record is three production and engineering credits, plus three further credits that survive only in video titles. This profile publishes exactly that, role by role, and invents nothing.
# Sources used:
# - Shazam, BRG Hollywood feat. Gwada G "WTHelly Bouyon" (opened 2026-10-20, credits also in the search index of the same page): single released May 16, 2025, label BankrollGang, BPM 164, language English; songwriters Jaheim Malakai Meyers and Brad M Douglas; producers Xavvoknockin and Xavern Labega; Knockin Records credited for Mix Mastering and as Recording Engineer. The producer name is spelled Xavvoknockin, one word, on this page.
# - YouTube, General Pye feat. Ebony Empress "Largent" (Bouyon 2026) (search result, opened description 2026-10-20): produced by Fr3EzE, Mixed and Mastered by Xavvoknockin, spelled Xavvoknockin in the description. Shazam song page for the same record (opened 2026-10-20): released October 13, 2025, label Arctic Willow Firm, BPM 130, songwriter Jeremy Chaloner Reed, producer Fr3eze; the Shazam credits do not list the mix and master role, so that role is carried here on the YouTube description only.
# - Tubidy video listing page (search result, 2026-10-20): a listing of Trixta Savage videos whose titles carry the credit Prod. by XavvoKnockin, in the camel case form XavvoKnockin, on "Bad Man" feat. JodyBree and on "Believe In Love" feat. Young OB, and Prod. by XavvoKnockin on "A Hundred" (Official Audio). Used only as video title credits, never as platform song page credits: no dated song page for these three titles was opened during this research.
# - Shazam, D4A Nillio "Storybook Riddim Freestyle (feat. Young Ob) [Bouyon Version]" (search result, 2026-10-20): released December 8, 2025, label Knockin Records, BPM 160. Used only to document that the name Knockin Records also circulates as a label name in the same bouyon circuit; no source consulted states who owns or runs Knockin Records, and no link between the label and the producer is asserted here beyond the shared name.
# - This site, BRG Hollywood profile (wave 4 parity, 2026-10-20): BRG Hollywood is Jaheim Meyers, a bouyon artist from Sint Maarten, first music artist from the Dutch side of Sint Maarten to reach one million YouTube views with "We Not Going Home" feat. C4, and a Bouyon Artist of the Year finalist at the Caribbean Music Awards 2026. Used as the verified context of the "WTHelly Bouyon" credit, not as a fact about Xavvoknockin himself.
# Note: no source consulted gives a full name, an origin, a date of birth or an official account for Xavvoknockin. His own island is therefore not stated as fact anywhere in this profile: what is documented is the scene his credits sit in, Sint Maarten and its bouyon circuit. sameAs stays empty, and the schema track list holds only the two recordings verified on a song page or an official video description.

